{"word":"chi","ipa":"kaɪ","persianMeaning":"انرژی حیات گردشی که در فلسفه چینی در تمام چیزها وجود دارد، بیست و دومین حرف الفبای یونانی","englishDefinition":"the circulating life energy that in Chinese philosophy is thought to be inherent in all things; in traditional Chinese medicine the balance of negative and positive forms in the body is believed to be essential for good health","partOfSpeech":"noun","example":"Acupuncture is based on the idea that chi flows through your body.","examplePersian":"در طب سنتی چینی، تعادل چی مثبت و منفی برای سلامتی ضروری است.","cefrLevel":"C2","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"wordFamily":[],"commonMistakes":"","ieltsRelevance":"Low","toeflRelevance":"Low","greRelevance":"Low","tags":["General","CEFR","offline","Openjam","needs-collocation"],"source":"Openjam + ECDICT + EnglishToPersianDictionaries","sourceLicense":"Openjam MIT; ECDICT MIT; EnglishToPersianDictionaries Apache-2.0","frequencyRank":7660,"examPriority":0,"learningOrder":376}
